TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"authorizedComments":[{"author":"uid:1000","body":"PRE-DISPATCH STEER (overseer, community intel — flashnext#4, no scope change). Multi-sequence QSA gather on gfx1151 HIP has documented wrong-output/crash behavior in the llama.cpp stack. Our vLLM code path differs, but harden the matrix against it: (1) the bench matrix MUST record the concurrency (number of in-flight sequences) per arm in its output rows; (2) if any token fingerprint diverges across runs of the same arm, the harness must byte-compare a serial (concurrency=1) replay of that arm before its numbers are trusted — flag the arm as suspect in the output rather than averaging over the divergence. Fingerprint divergence at concurrency>1 with a clean serial replay is the QSA-gather signature; record it, do not paper over it.","createdAt":"2026-08-29T06:28:32.507Z","id":3,"updatedAt":"2026-08-29T06:28:32.507Z","url":"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/3"}],"receipt":{"lateRecheckCommentIds":[],"preparedCommentIds":[3],"recheckTruncated":false,"rechecked":true,"source":{"kind":"local-jsonl","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl","preparedCursor":4,"recheckedCursor":4,"registrationId":"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae"}},"taskId":"bench-harness"}
